+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
+Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:15:00 -0500
+Subject: [PATCH 7/7] [VideoPlayer] DRM PRIME: composite subtitles into the
+ Dolby Vision signal
+
+In standard Dolby Vision the sink decodes every pixel of the tunnel
+frame as the packed 12-bit signal, so subtitles the display blends over
+it from the GUI plane come out in the wrong colours: white text turns
+purple.
+
+Let a renderer draw the overlays into the video itself
+(CBaseRenderer::RenderOverlays). While the tunnel is used,
+CRendererDRMPRIME draws them into an offscreen buffer of the GUI's size,
+a dma-buf, and libpi_engine composites them into the picture's signal,
+which also reports the whole picture as the active area while they are
+shown. The overlays report the area they draw (COverlay::GetBounds), so
+the engine composites only there. A change over a paused picture
+renders it again.
+
+Signed-off-by: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
